at this point I think it's safe to say  that every Mortal Kombat has a big bad  villain an antagonist who drives the  main story forward the final boss of the  game with MK 11 we have the introduction  of Kronecker who is referred to as a  Titan a species that we've never seen  before that ranked even higher than the  Elder Gods in terms of power and status  there aren't many who were aware of the  Titans existence outside of Shao Kahn  and Raiden who up until they encountered  Kronecker believed them to be nothing  more than made-up stories a race of  beings who manipulate an influence time  unbeknownst to everyone else Kronecker  herself is referred to as the architect  of the destiny within the universe  meaning whatever happens and has  happened she already predetermined it's  difficult to describe her as purely evil  because what she desires is a balance  between good and evil within the  universe which does raise the question  why have we never seen her before the  explanation that were given relates to  her children shinnok and setri on  Sherlock being the god of death and  darkness and setri on the goddess of  life and light essentially makes them  each other's counterpart to the mother  these opposing ideas create an  equilibrium a perfect balance between  the two it is worth mentioning that she  doesn't really seem to care about her  children they just kind of exists to  help her create this truly balanced  universe however this balance is broken  when shinnok is beheaded and so  Kronecker decides that she must then  restart the entire timeline from the  beginning the power of altering time and  causing the past and present to collide  is just one of the many things that  Kronecker is capable of and Raiden does  mention that up until now she has  actually done this several times before  she is also capable of manipulating the  sands shooting beams of energy and  telekinesis  despite this her power isn't unlimited  and she can't just reset the timelines  whenever she wants to in order to use  her hourglass she must first draw power  from the earth roms life force and we do  also see her using Shang Tsung's Chronos  dolls to enhance her power further you  definitely can make the point that  Kronecker isn't your ordinary villain  because she has this higher calling that  isn't innately evil but she still is a  very unlikable character and not just  because she floats around wearing this  stupid piece of metal but because she's  completely obsessed of the idea of  balance anyone who disagrees with her  gets in the way of her perfect division  is essentially erased from history when  the timeline resets if we also consider  that everything happens because  Kronecker allows it to happen  then that does mean she's responsible  for everything good but that also means  that she has no problem watching and  recreating the same atrocities and acts  of evil  whenever the timeline is reset Kern  occurs most powerful ability is her  manipulation of time itself we see this  pretty early on when she brings  individuals from past timelines into the  present with the promise of a better  life if they assist her we then find out  that Raiden in his quest to defend Earth  room from evil has become cronikeys  biggest hurdle to achieve in this  perfect imbalance after Raiden behead  she knock an MK 10 that is essentially  the final straw Kronecker comes out of  hiding and decides to reset the timeline  once again Raiden is one of chronic ha's  biggest threats but alone he simply  cannot defeat her and this is where Liu  Kang comes into the story what she fears  the most is Liu Kang and Raiden working  together to stop her which is why in  every previous timeline there is a  conflict between the two which ends in  Liu Kang's death during this year story  Raiden begins to have flashbacks from  previous timelines and they are able to  prevent history from repeating itself  this year Raiden and Liu Kang then work  together do their weird little fusion  dance and become a fire Thunder demigod  and defeat Kronecker just as she once  feared with his new powers Liu Kang  becomes the new keeper of time and  discharged with rebuilding the timeline  from the very beginning there's no doubt  that this year story has divided opinion  and has some mixed reviews there are  some good ideas and then there are some  so good but I do like when it sets up  for the next game whether or not  kuroneko's going to stay dead do we  don't really know but with her  introduction into the story I think it's  fair to assume that there may be more  Titans than just Kronecker and maybe her  death will spark some kind of  retaliation from the rest of them if the  Titans are then going to be the main  villains of MK 12 it's reasonable to  believe that all of the current  characters would have to band together  and Liu Kang may have to bring back  previous characters from other timelines  could this mean MK 12 is going to bring  back characters from previous games if  not have an entire playable roster from  the entire franchise I don't know and if  I know NetherRealm neither do they but  let me know what your thoughts are
 

